{"format":"mathslides","version":1,"deck":{"version":1,"id":"P6-wnMsv62","title":"ppo-grpo","slides":[{"id":"aSzAFecJvj","background":"#ffffff","elements":[{"id":"hUmARujtb4","type":"text","x":84,"y":30,"w":332,"h":43,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"From PPO to GRPO"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":32,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"r4S13QFerJ","type":"text","x":84,"y":98,"w":1188,"h":97,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) (Schulman et al., 2017) is an actor-critic RL algorithm that is widely used in the RL fine-tuning stage of LLMs (Ouyang et al., 2022). In particular, it optimizes LLMs by maximizing the following surrogate objective:"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":24,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"F-IpKT8w0u","type":"text","x":127,"y":195,"w":1065,"h":76,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"mathBlock","attrs":{"latex":"J_{PPO}(\\theta) = \\mathbb{E}[q \\sim P(Q), o \\sim \\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(O|q)] \\frac{1}{|o|} \\sum_{t=1}^{|o|} \\min \\left[ \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})} A_t, \\text{clip} \\left( \\frac{\\pi_{\\theta}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}{\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}(o_t|q, o_{<t})}, 1-\\varepsilon, 1+\\varepsilon \\right) A_t \\right],"}}]},"style":{"fontSize":20,"color":"#000000","align":"center","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}},{"id":"sEDdCsQqxJ","type":"text","x":137,"y":298,"w":1135,"h":108,"doc":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"where "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi_{\\theta}"}},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}"}},{"type":"text","text":" are the current and old policy models, and "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"q, o"}},{"type":"text","text":" are questions and outputs sampled from the question dataset and the old policy "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\pi_{\\theta_{old}}"}},{"type":"text","text":", respectively. "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"\\varepsilon"}},{"type":"text","text":" is a clipping-related hyper-parameter introduced in PPO for stabilizing training. "},{"type":"mathInline","attrs":{"latex":"A_t"}},{"type":"text","text":" is the advantage, which is computed by applying Generalized Advantage Estimation (GAE) (Schulman et al., 2015), based"}]}]},"style":{"fontSize":20,"color":"#000000","align":"left","lineHeight":1.35,"fill":null}}],"notes":"","reference":""}]},"assets":{}}